      "layer": 11,
      "visible": true,
      "locked": false,
      "description": "Create a 64x64 top-down 2D cooking game asset of a food pickup counter / serving station.\nThis object is used in a restaurant cooking game as the place where finished dishes appear after cooking. The gameplay purpose is clear: when food is completed, it is placed on this counter, and the player walks over to pick it up.\nDesign the asset in a top-down cooking game style, similar to casual restaurant management and kitchen games. The counter should look like a functional serving station, not just decoration. It must immediately communicate to the player that this is the place for ready-to-pick-up food.\nThe asset should include:\n- a clear countertop surface,\n- a compact counter body,\n- 2 to 3 visible serving spots on top where completed food can appear,\n- simple kitchen or serving details that support the function,\n- enough empty space on the top surface so food sprites can be placed later.\nThe style should be:\n- 2D top-down game asset,\n- cartoon / casual cooking game style,\n- clean and readable,\n- simple shapes,\n- strong silhouette,\n- slightly colorful,\n- cozy restaurant atmosphere,\n- suitable for a 64x64 sprite,\n- easy to recognize in gameplay at small size.\nThe counter may be made of:\n- wood,\n- stainless steel,\n- diner-style restaurant material,\n  depending on a cozy kitchen theme.\nOptional small details:\n- a serving tray,\n- subtle plate placement marks,\n- a tiny serving bell,\n- small warm lamp detail,\n- clean front panel,\n- slight highlights to separate the countertop from the base.\nImportant design rules:\n- keep the top surface mostly empty,\n- do not permanently place too much food on it,\n- do not add characters,\n- do not include a full kitchen background,\n- do not add large text,\n- do not overload the sprite with tiny details,\n- make the object readable and functional first.\nThe visual idea should clearly show this gameplay loop:\ncook food \u2192 finished dish appears on the counter \u2192 player walks there \u2192 player picks it up.\nThe final result should be:\n- a single standalone 2D sprite,\n- transparent background,\n- ready to use in a top-down cooking game,\n- designed for a 64x64 tile,\n- readable, clean, and game-friendly.\nKeywords: 64x64 sprite, top-down cooking game, serving counter, food pickup station, ready dish counter, restaurant game asset, kitchen object, cartoon 2D sprite, transparent background.",
